      "content": "i get what you're saying about the traffic and finances, but that's almost the point. the \"intensity\" isn't just people walking around. look at the way the streets converge at that specific angle near the Battery. it's not a standard right angle grid. if you look at the geometry of those specific intersections, doesn't it feel like they were mathematically optimized to act as a focal point? why do you think the planners chose those specific angles instead of just following a strict orthogonal grid everywhere?",
